
==============================================================================================================
S1  THE RELATION, STEP BY STEP
==============================================================================================================
  H0 = 67.4 km/s/Mpc = 2.18429e-18 s^-1
  rho_crit = 3 H0^2/(8 pi G) = 8.5329e-27 kg m^-3
  rho_Lambda = Omega_Lambda rho_crit = 5.8450e-27 kg m^-3        (Omega_Lambda = 0.685)
  G rho_Lambda = 3.9011e-37 s^-2 ;  sqrt = 6.2459e-19 s^-1
  c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) = 1.8725e-10 m s^-2      <- the unique acceleration built from (c, G, rho_Lambda)
  kappa = 1/2:  a0 = 9.3624e-11 m s^-2   (rho_Lambda);   1.1312e-10 m s^-2   (rho_crit);  ratio 1.2082 = 1/sqrt(Omega_Lambda)
  H_Lambda = H0 sqrt(Omega_Lambda) = 1.80782e-18 s^-1 ;  c H_Lambda = 5.4197e-10 ;  c H0 = 6.5483e-10 m s^-2
  Lambda = 3 H_Lambda^2/c^2 = 1.0909e-52 m^-2 ;  de Sitter radius c/H_Lambda = 1.6583e+26 m = 5.37 Gpc
  Z = c H_Lambda / a0 = 5.7888 ;  sqrt(32 pi/3) = 5.7888
  four forms: (c/2)sqrt(G rho_L) = 9.362375e-11;  c^2 sqrt(Lambda/32pi) = 9.362375e-11;  cH_L/sqrt(32pi/3) = 9.362375e-11;  c^2/(sqrt(32pi/3) R_dS) = 9.362375e-11
  natural units: M_Lambda = rho_Lambda^(1/4) = 2.240 meV ;  M_P = 1.2209e+28 eV ;  M_Lambda^2/(2 M_P) -> 9.362375e-11 m s^-2
  l0 = c^2/a0 = 9.5996e+26 m ;  Lambda l0^2 = 100.5310 ;  32 pi = 100.5310
  [PASS] S1a the four forms of the kappa = 1/2 relation are one number   (max relative difference 2.2e-16)
  [PASS] S1b Z = sqrt(32 pi/3) identically (no data content: H cancels)   (Z = 5.788810)
  [PASS] S1c a0(rho_Lambda) = 9.36e-11 and a0(rho_crit) = 1.13e-10 to three figures   (9.3624e-11, 1.1312e-10)

