==============================================================================================================
S5  THE CLOSED-FORM INVERSION OF THE RC100 DARK-MATTER FRACTIONS
==============================================================================================================
  a0 = (1 - f_DM) g_obs / [ln(1/f_DM)]^2 for 99 of 100 galaxies (f_DM in (0.02, 0.98)); z = 0.61 - 2.52
  median a0 = 1.385e-10 m s^-2;  16-84%: 5.22e-11 - 3.46e-10;  median y = 1.45
  accelerations probed: y = g_bar/a0 16/50/84% = 0.33/1.45/5.30;  15 of 99 below 0.3;  A_obs there = 2.7/3.9/7.8
  d log10 a0/dz = -0.1123 +/- 0.0626 (bootstrap);  constant: 0 (-1.8 sigma);  halo-emergent mean slope +0.1311 (-3.9 sigma);  H(z) mean slope +0.2304 (-5.5 sigma)
  what drives it: d log10 f_DM/dz = -0.140  (the published fall of the dark-matter fraction with redshift); the inversion is monotone in f_DM
  scatter about the fit: 0.38 dex;  corr(log a0_hat, log y_hat) = -0.73  (noise in f_DM moves a0_hat and y_hat oppositely)
  controlling for log g_obs (measured, a0-free):   d log a0/dz = -0.138 +/- 0.063   -> halo-emergent mean slope disfavoured at 4.3 sigma
  controlling for log y_hat (absorbs noise AND part of any real signal): +0.008 +/- 0.048   -> 2.6 sigma
  weakest exclusion of the H(z) mean slope over the three treatments: 4.7 sigma
  range of the redshift slope over the three treatments: -0.14 to +0.01;  weakest exclusion of the halo-emergent slope: 2.6 sigma
  [PASS] S5a the inversion is exact: nu(y) (1 - f_DM) = 1 at y = [ln(1/f_DM)]^2
  [PASS] S5b the RC100 trend is consistent with constant a0 within 2.5 sigma and more than 3 sigma below the halo-emergent mean slope   (-0.112 +/- 0.063)
  [PASS] S5c no decline is claimed: the slope is within 2.5 sigma of zero under every treatment
  [PASS] S5d AGAINST INTEREST: the 3.9 sigma does not survive every control -- the weakest exclusion of the halo-emergent slope is below 3 sigma, and that is the number to quote   (weakest 2.6 sigma)

